<!--
  The launcher icon, foreground layer: a balance beam with a slice of pie on one side and a dumbbell on the
  other. The geometry is generated by tools/icon_design.py — that script is the source of these coordinates, so
  the approved preview and the shipped vector cannot drift apart.

  Three things this drawing obeys, all forced by the 24 dp case (docs/04-plan.md, M7.4):
  * the beam carries the meaning, so there are no pans: at 24 dp they collapsed into the objects;
  * the slice and the dumbbell differ in OUTLINE — a wedge tipped with a golden crust against a bar with two
    plates — so they stay distinguishable in greyscale and at small sizes, where colour alone would not;
  * the slice has depth (a dark cut face below the top face) so it reads as a piece of something rather than
    a flat triangle.

  Colours: ink structure, steel-blue dumbbell (#4682B4, the owner's choice), and the pie in two tones —
  golden crust over berry filling — because one flat amber read as a blob.
-->
